# Scratch queue rows TPF (plan_process_overhaul.md P2.1). Data: the queue table in scratch_queue.md is generated
# from this file (python3 tools/status_index.py). Format: tools/scratch_query/qrows.py docstring.
# Run: qrun.py run OUT feature_writeup/testing/rows/TPF.qb RES [--section KEY] [--rows ID,...]

@@section 1
@@title SQ-TPF Third-party bug fixes: Packet Fixer and Debugify Reforged, 2026-11-13 ([thirdparty_fixes.md](../thirdparty_fixes.md) sections 2 and 7, TODO `largecontent/mod-additions #80`)
@@date 2026-11-13
@@jars creativecommon
@@sources feature_writeup/thirdparty_fixes.md
@@prep spawn-animals=true spawn-npcs=true
@@text
@@text Targets `packetfixer-3.3.2-1.18-1.20.4-merged.jar` and `debugify-1.1.0-forge-1.19.2.jar`. Both are in the
@@text instance's `mods/` since 2026-11-13 23:20. Packet Fixer has a `both` row since 2026-11-13 (shipped to clients and server with one
@@text bounded config): `prep_srv.sh` and `eval_client.py setup` copy it into every scratch server and client, so rows that
@@text need a side without it delete it from `srv/mods` or `GAME/mods`. Debugify has a `both` row and ships `config/debugify.json` (9 fixes) since 2026-11-14 (plan_bugfix_1114.md 2); rows that write their own config still overwrite it per boot. `prep_srv.sh` copies the jar into every scratch server: rows that need a side WITHOUT one delete it from `OUT/srv/mods` (or `GAME/mods`) before the boot; reference
@@text copies in `jar_archive/thirdparty_fixes/`. Write the Debugify and Packet Fixer configs into the scratch dir every boot
@@text (the instance `debugify.json` is the shipped set since 2026-11-14; Packet Fixer's instance file is unlimited). Phases, boots and setup: thirdparty_fixes.md section 7 (P1 to P7). Debugify config per boot:
@@text `tools/scratch_query/tpf_debugify_cfg.py CONFIG/debugify.json [@set ...]` (no set = every fix off). Probe:
@@text `tools/scratch_query/tpf_probe.js` as `zz_tpf_probe.js` (written, not yet run). Every fix row runs twice: "base" (fix
@@text off: the bug must reproduce) and "fix" (its tranche on: the bug must be gone); a fix whose base does not reproduce stays
@@text off (thirdparty_fixes.md rule 2). Server batches ready: `tools/scratch_query/batches/r1113tpf/s1_base.qb` and
@@text `s1_fix.qb` (generated from `s1_common.inc` by `s1_gen.py`); client batches are written by the runner from these rows.
@@text
@@table
## SQ-TPF-00 | setup and boot: both jars load, no mixin errors from them
@group A
@commands `s1_base.qb` / `s1_fix.qb` row SQ-TPF-00: boot with both jars, gamerules, forceload; prints both configs. Rerun 2026-11-14 with the shipped `config/debugify.json` (9 fixes on; plan_bugfix_1114.md 2): also `grep "Enabled [0-9]*/" logs/latest.log`
@pass `Enabled N/..` with N the server-side count of the 9 shipped fixes; no `Mixin apply failed`, `InvalidInjectionException`, `MixinTransformerError`; log names debugify and packetfixer; `config/packetfixer.properties` generated (record its defaults for SQ-TPF-30)
@fails mixin error naming debugify/packetfixer: a clash with an installed mixin (thirdparty_fixes.md 6 lists the shared targets)
@from batches/r1113tpf/s1_fix.qb passed
bootreject Mixin apply failed|InvalidMixinException|InvalidInjectionException|MixinTransformerError
bootexpect (?i)debugify
bootexpect (?i)packetfixer
> gamerule doFireTick false
> gamerule doMobSpawning false
> gamerule doDaylightCycle false
> time set 6000
> difficulty normal
> forceload add 1000 1000 1599 1015
sleep 8
shell cat config/packetfixer.properties config/debugify.json | tr '\n' ' ' | head -c 600
shell grep -ciE "debugify|packetfixer" logs/latest.log; true

## SQ-TPF-01 | shipped debugify.json: boot Done, no MC-121706 crash, 9 fixes applied; file unchanged by the boot
@group A
@commands Rewritten 2026-11-14 (plan_bugfix_1114.md 2): the SHIPPED file. Copy the instance `config/debugify.json` into the scratch `config/` unchanged (no `tpf_debugify_cfg.py` call); `sha1sum` it; boot; `grep -E "Enabled [0-9]+/|Mixin apply failed|mc121706" logs/latest.log`; after `stop`, `diff` the scratch file against `configs_edited/root_config/debugify.json`; then `s1_fix.qb`
